> > > > > > > > > > > > > > > >
> > > > > > > > > > > > > > > > The biggest challenge I am running into right now is dealing with the random intercepts.
> > > > > > > > > > > > > > > >
> > > > > > > > > > > > > > > > > lm.null = lmer(PROP ~ FOOD + (1+FOOD|MOUSEID) + (1+FOOD|SITE), data = finalset, REML=FALSE)
> > > > > > > > > > > > > > > > maxfun < 10 * length(par)^2 is not recommended.convergence code 1 from bobyqa: bobyqa -- maximum number of function evaluations exceededmaxfun < 10 * length(par)^2 is not recommended.convergence code 1 from bobyqa: bobyqa -- maximum number of function evaluations exceededunable to evaluate scaled gradientModel failed to converge: degenerate  Hessian with 2 negative eigenvalues>
> > > > > > > > > > > > > > > > > lm.null2 = lmer(PROP ~ FOOD + (1+FOOD|MOUSEID) + (1|SITE), data = finalset, REML=FALSE)
