Hi D-RUGgies,

Hope you are all doing well. Please come by the Library in Room 360 tomorrow at 10am for our usual R work session. Since tomorrow is International Baby Day, I thought it might be fun to demo the babynames package. Or just come and work on something you are interested in.

More importantly, if you aren't sure where Shields Library Room 360* is, I've made a treasure pirate map you can use to navigate with. As you can tell, it's extremely accurate and drawn to scale. R was not used in creating this map, but my 5-year old did provide some helpful suggestions.

The schedule for the remainder of the quarter looks like this...but we may shift things around as needed. If you'd like to give a talk or have theme ideas, please let me know! If I can find a package or data that corresponds with the day, I plan on giving a little 5-10 min demo, just for fun.

SPRING 2017 D-RUG SCHEDULE (10am-12pm, Shields 360 in DSI)
May 9: Using RStudio/RMarkdown to create and maintain your CV (Ryan)
May 16: International Drawing Day: follow-up on GIS in R, intro to "sf" package for spatial data
May 23: Regular work session, International Turtle Day
May 30: Working with rasters in R (Eric Holmes)
June 6: Regular work session, International Yo-Yo day
Thanks,
Adios,
Ryan
