It's now possible to install R (and RStudio) through Anaconda <https://www.continuum.io/anaconda-overview>. Managing your R packages using Conda <https://conda.io/docs/> should ease dependency management and circumvent these frustrating build issues.

No promises, but this could be an easy solution (rJava <https://anaconda.org/r/r-rjava> is available through the conda R channel <https://anaconda.org/r/>).

Check out:
