Hi Folks,

Sorry forgot to record/webcast the presentation on making a CV using RMarkdown. However, if you want to see the source material, it's on github here:
https://github.com/ryanpeek/markdown_cv
I essentially took Steven Miller's excellent post <http://svmiller.com/blog/2016/03/svm-r-markdown-cv/> and associated code <https://github.com/svmiller/svm-r-markdown-templates> and utilized it with a few minor formatting changes.

Important tips:
Use a new RStudio project for this (and everything, it makes things easier)
Make sure you have a LaTex distribution installed (see here <http://www.latex-project.org/get/>, note: it is a big file and will take a little time to install the first time)
Make sure in your RStudio global settings you have pdfLaTex selected in the Sweave options (see here <https://support.rstudio.com/hc/en-us/articles/200532257-Customizing-LaTeX-Options> for more info on checking this)
The RMarkdown (.Rmd) file (in my repo, I have a few versions) needs to be in the same place as the .tex file, which is the template that is used to render the document into a nice PDF.

